      "ref": "TMA1995/s52",
      "quote": "(2) The notice of opposition must be filed: (a) in accordance with the regulations; and (b) within the prescribed period, or within that period as extended in accordance with the regulations or in accordance with subsection (5)."
    },
    {
      "ref": "TMM/Part47/1/1/3/2",
      "quote": "The application for an extension of time to file a notice of intention to oppose or a statement of grounds and particulars must be filed with the Trade Marks Office in an approved form and accompanied by the relevant fee (see item 6 in Schedule 9 of the Trade Marks Regulations 1995). The application will not be processed until the fee is paid."
    },
    {
      "ref": "TMM/Part47/1/1/3/2",
      "quote": "A form is available on IP Australia’s website. An opponent is not required to use this form however it may be useful as a guide."
